  "summary": "An SFPD compliance audit uncovered 299 improper queries of the department's Flock-based license plate reader database by Western States Information Network analysts who had been granted nighttime access through NCRIC without SFPD's knowledge. Chief Derrick Lew disabled NCRIC and WSIN access; officials said no ICE or immigration-related queries were found. The disclosure follows prior reporting that out-of-state agencies, including a Georgia sheriff and Dallas PD, ran over 1.6 million searches of SFPD data.",
  "key_quotes": [
    {
      "quote": "The San Francisco Police Department said it uncovered 299 improper inquiries within what it described as \u201cover roughly a year\u201d through a routine compliance audit in May",
      "paragraph_idx": 5
    },
    {
      "quote": "NCRIC had granted the network\u2019s Watch Center access to the city\u2019s data during night hours without the SFPD\u2019s knowledge",
      "paragraph_idx": 10
    },
    {
      "quote": "Police Chief Derrick Lew disabled NCRIC\u2019s access upon discovering the searches and opened an internal review",
      "paragraph_idx": 12
    }
  ],
